+## Uploaders
+
+The OTel plugin supports pluggable upload backends:
+
+| Uploader | Backend | Selected when |
+|---|---|---|
+| `MlflowProtobufUploader` | MLflow | `MLFLOW_EXPERIMENT_NAME` / `MLFLOW_TRACKING_TOKEN` set (default) |
+| `LangfuseUploader` | Langfuse (self-hosted or cloud) | `LANGFUSE_PUBLIC_KEY` set |
+
+### Langfuse
+
+```bash
+export LANGFUSE_HOST="https://langfuse.example.com"
+export LANGFUSE_PUBLIC_KEY="pk-lf-..."
+export LANGFUSE_SECRET_KEY="sk-lf-..."
+harbor run ... --plugin atif2otel
+```
+
+Spans are exported to `{LANGFUSE_HOST}/api/public/otel/v1/traces` (OTLP/HTTP, protobuf) with HTTP Basic auth and the `x-langfuse-ingestion-version: 4` header, which enables real-time ingestion on Langfuse v4 (without it, directly-ingested OTel data can be delayed by up to 10 minutes). Transient server errors (408/429/5xx) are retried with exponential backoff. `LANGFUSE_HOST` also satisfies the plugin's endpoint requirement in `auto` mode, so no `OTEL_EXPORTER_OTLP_ENDPOINT` is needed.
+
+Direct use:
+
+```python
+from harbor_atif2otel.uploaders.langfuse import LangfuseUploader
+
+uploader = LangfuseUploader(
+    host="https://langfuse.example.com",
+    public_key="pk-lf-...",
+    secret_key="sk-lf-...",
+)
+uploader.upload(resource_spans)
+```
+
